# Last OPL music note keeps playing forever on core reboot

- Source URL: https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/ao486_MiSTer/issues/174

Hello there,

I noticed that, as the tittle says, if a program is playing an OPL music note an the core is reboot, that last note keeps sounding forever, until a new program resets the OPL.

@humply Can you see this bug too?

## Fetched Issue/PR Details

Title: OPL3: fix envelope RELEASE state on reset (PR #188)

Description: The pull request addresses a regression introduced in commit e881af1 where envelopes should transition to RELEASE state instead of remaining in SUSTAIN, causing notes to play indefinitely after reset. The fix involves resetting the key-on signal itself, as it is no longer edge-detected. Closes issue #174.

Status: Merged by sorgelig on Feb 24, 2025

Comments:
- gtaylormb (Feb 23, 2025): Provided the original description with context about the regression and fix approach.
- vanfanel (Feb 25, 2025): "Sadly this doesn't fix #174 completely, a low-frequency tone keeps playing after resetting an OPL game." Reports that despite the merge, a residual tone persists after core reset via CTRL+ALT+SUP in games like Prince of Persia, though menu-based resets work correctly.

